the difference between count and for_each in terraform practically 

* Count it will create multiple instances if you give count = n here n is number 1 2 3 etc

* for_each also will do the same as a count but it will accept a map or a set of string 

* If you want to create a t2.micro instance for app and t2.medium for web we can use

Example :

type        = map(string)
  default = {
    web  = "t2.micro"
    app  = "t2.medium"
    db   = "t2.large"
  }

* If you want to create one instance for Jenkins one for docker and one more ansible for that also you can use for_each
